-- R39 - ASIA RATES: a daily block in both Takeaways on Asia government bond and swap moves (1d/3d/1w bp), curves,
-- swap spreads, a LOCAL vs GLOBAL read, a candidate expression with invalidation, and commentary leads.
-- Source: thread "Add Asia rates to Macro Takeaways", 26 Nov 2026 (owner: "Is it possible to some way capture the market
-- moves in Asia rates too ... that would make it quite a complete digest for me"). Data: market pack section J
-- (scripts/marketpack/marketpack.py, from the 27 Nov build). The id is assigned by dash.propose_rule. Put in force the same day by
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R39' and status = 'proposed';
-- "revert R39" removes it. The call below is the exact call that was run.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "ASIA RATES block every day: Asia govvies and swaps with 1d/3d/1w bp moves, curves, swap spreads, a LOCAL vs GLOBAL read, a candidate expression with invalidation, and commentary leads", "body": "ASIA RATES (owner's ask 26 Nov 2026: \"Asia rates aren't captured anywhere, and the last 2-3 sessions saw the biggest rally in a lot of Asia rates like MYR, THB, TWD, SGD and JPY\"; capture the daily moves and good commentary).\n\n1. INPUT. Section J of the market pack (ASIA RATES), read in the same pass as sections A, D, H and I: J1 government bonds (JGB, KTB, CGB, SGS, IGB, INDOGB, MGS, ThaiGB, TGB, RPGB, HKGB), J2 swaps from DTCC prints (JPY TONA, SGD SORA, KRW CD, TWD TAIBOR, CNY repo, THB THOR, MYR KLIBOR, HKD HIBOR, INR MIBOR), the MOVERS and CURVES lines, J3 commentary. Missing or stale pack: print \"ASIA RATES: pack section J missing\" and nothing else in the block. Never web-search to fill a level or change that J lacks; \"n/a\" stays n/a. A swap row marked \"thin\" (n<3) is never cited.\n\n2. WHERE. Its own block with the heading ASIA RATES, printed straight after DOLLAR DRIVERS and before the first theme. At most seven lines, about 1,300 characters. Under R33 it is never trimmed; if the email is over budget the R33 order is applied to the other sections. Under R38 it takes the same styling as DOLLAR DRIVERS: the <h2> band; a line gets the amber bar with its decisive numbers bold when any cited move is 5bp or more in 1d, 15bp or more in 1w, or a sig of 2.0 or more; grey when quiet. R38's READ FIRST box gets one more line, ASIA RATES, after USD, copied from line (a).\n\n3. LINES, each one line, numbers from J with their as-of dates (changes in bp, written 1d / 3d / 1w):\n(a) MOVERS: the biggest rallies and sell-offs from J's MOVERS line, and whether the move is broad (how many of the 10Y govvies fell vs rose on 1d and 1w) or local.\n(b) JAPAN: JGB 2Y, 10Y, 30Y and TONA 5Y/10Y; the 2s10s change; JGB-minus-swap change when it moved 3bp or more.\n(c) NORTH ASIA: KTB 3Y/10Y with KRW CD 5Y; CGB 10Y with CNY repo 5Y; TGB 10Y with TWD TAIBOR 5Y; HKD 5Y when it moved 5bp or more.\n(d) ASEAN AND INDIA: SGS 10Y with SORA 5Y; MGS 10Y with MYR KLIBOR 5Y; ThaiGB 10Y with THOR 5Y; RPGB 10Y; INDOGB 10Y; IGB 10Y with MIBOR OIS 5Y.\n(e) READ: in two sentences, what is driving it (UST and global duration, local policy pricing or a dated meeting, FX and flows, oil), checked against sections A, I and the theme set: name it LOCAL when Asia moved more than USTs over the same window, GLOBAL BETA otherwise. Then where consensus and positioning sit and the pain trade.\n(f) EXPRESSION: the candidate trade if one stands out (receive or pay, which tenor or curve, outright or vs another market, rough r/r) and INVALIDATION as a named level or datum. It is a candidate, not a card: an Asia rates card still goes through the gate, R09, R14 and R31.\n(g) COMMENTARY: up to three leads from J3, with source names, chosen for rates content (a central-bank operation or auction result, a research note, a press report on the move). A lead is checked at its source before the block repeats a claim from it; an unchecked one is named as a lead only.\n\n4. LIMITS. Evidence only: the block never raises or lowers p by itself and never opens or closes a card. Trading Economics levels print to 0.01, so its 3d/1w changes are good to about 1bp; DTCC swaps are a US-reported sample (say \"DTCC sample\" when a swap level carries an argument). Mixed sources: the official curves (MOF, ECOS, ChinaMoney) are constant-maturity or curve yields, not benchmark bonds; compare changes, not levels, across sources.\n\n5. FOOTER. The market pack line ends \"· J <status>\" as section J's status prints it.", "rationale": "The owner noticed Asia rates appear nowhere in the Takeaways while MYR, THB, TWD, SGD and JPY rates had their biggest rally in a while. The prompts are at their byte cap, so the block goes in as a rule fed by new market pack section J, built and tested in the thread on 26 Nov. That morning's read: JGB 10Y -20bp and KTB 10Y -21bp on 1w, TONA 5Y -23bp; TWD 5Y -17bp, THOR 5Y -15bp, SORA 5Y -12bp, MYR 5Y -7bp; CGB flat.", "evidence": "Market pack section J built 26 Nov 2026 from Japan MOF, Bank of Korea ECOS (public sample key), ChinaMoney CGB curve, Trading Economics country pages and DTCC CFTC rates files; commentary from BOJ and RBI RSS, ING Think RSS and Google News.", "revert_if": "Revert if the block is missing or misread on three days in two weeks, or if the owner says it adds nothing to his own read.", "review_due": "2026-12-21", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
